      ":question/problem": "A statement of the intermediate value theorem is given below but some of its parts are missing.\n\n> *Let $f(x)$ be a function that is $______$ on a closed interval $[a, b]$. If $k$ is a number that lies between $_________$, then there exists a number $c \u2208 [a, b]$ such that $f(c) = k$.*\n\nGoing from left to right, in which order should the parts I-III listed below be placed into the blank spaces to complete the statement of the theorem?\n\n1. increasing\n2. continuous\n3. $f(a)$ and $f(b)$ inclusively"
